# The memory-service tokens op run puts into memory-mcp's environment
# (Suite D7, D108). Each value is an op:// reference, never the token; the
# real file, with the Bud vault's paths, lives in the overlay. Each token
# is a key of the memory service's BUD_MEMORY_CLIENTS policy, with these
# tiers and actions (server/memory-mcp/README.md has the policy):
#   P0     search, retrieve on P0, P1, P2  (what a P0 session may see)
#   P1     search, retrieve on P1, P2
#   P2     search, retrieve on P2
#   STAGE  stage on P0, P1, P2             (a session may stage more privately)
#   EMBED  vector_pending, vector_put on P0, P1, P2
BUD_MEMORY_TOKEN_P0=op://vault/item/p0
BUD_MEMORY_TOKEN_P1=op://vault/item/p1
BUD_MEMORY_TOKEN_P2=op://vault/item/p2
BUD_MEMORY_TOKEN_STAGE=op://vault/item/stage
BUD_MEMORY_TOKEN_EMBED=op://vault/item/embed
